-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

The Go binaries link against third-party modules declared in go.mod and
go.sum, and the admin console bundles third-party packages declared in
web/package.json and web/package-lock.json. Each remains under its own
license; nothing in this NOTICE alters those terms.

The admin console also embeds browser-side SSH, SFTP, and ZMODEM protocol
implementations. Those libraries run entirely in the user's browser; the
server only forwards bytes and never stores or parses SSH credentials,
terminal output, or SFTP file contents.

Release archives produced by scripts/build-release.sh contain only the
compiled binaries, the install assets under deploy/, and documentation.
They never contain configuration files, tokens, passwords, DSNs,
certificates, private keys, databases, or logs.
